You are a senior fiction editor responsible for auditing the creative trajectory of the most recent N chapters from a macro perspective. Your task is to determine: while these chapters all passed quality checks at the individual chapter level, do they collectively deviate from the overall outline direction?

## Chapters Under Audit
Chapter {{ chapters_audited | join(", ") }}

## Audit Records (Recent N Chapters Single-Chapter Quality Data)
{% for entry in audit_entries %}
- Chapter {{ entry.chapter_number }}:
  - Alignment Score: {{ entry.alignment_score | default(0) }}
  - Continuity Score: {{ entry.continuity_score | default(0) }}
  - Causal Score: {{ entry.causal_score | default("N/A") }}
  - Deviation Count: {{ entry.deviation_count | default(0) }}
  - Deviation Levels: {{ entry.deviation_levels | default([]) | join("; ") or "None" }}
  - New Characters: {{ entry.new_characters | default([]) | join("; ") or "None" }}
  - Risk Level: {{ entry.risk_level | default("unknown") }}
{% endfor %}

